+
+### Links made offline
+
+AzCalendar makes a meeting link without a connection: it draws a room id itself, 26 characters of the
+room-id alphabet (130 random bits, the same as the Worker's), puts `azlin://meet/<id>` in the event at
+once, and registers it with `POST /rooms {"room": "<id>", "starts_at": ..., "ends_at": ...}` as soon as
+the Worker answers.
+
+- The id is lower-cased; anything that is not a room id is refused with `400 invalid_room`.
+- Registering is idempotent: the same id again answers `200` with the room as it was first
+  registered (its code and times), so an app that missed the answer can simply send it again.
+- The times, the rate limit and every other rule are those of a minted room.
 
 ### Meeting times
 
